problems.description:
Read a line of text. Split it into words, tally how many times each word appears in a dictionary, and print the dictionary - the count a search index keeps for every term on a page.

Sample Input: apple banana apple
Expected Output: {'apple': 2, 'banana': 1}

Given two objects - one with an id, one with an email and a role - merge them with the spread operator, then destructure id, email and role out of the result and print a one-line summary.

Sample Input: {id: 1} {email: "a@b.com", role: "Dev"}
Expected Output: User #1: a@b.com (Dev)

Write an async function that awaits a simulated API call returning a status code and a JSON payload, wrapped in try...catch, and prints the response line - the capstone finale, reading the async result top to bottom with no callback nesting.

Sample Input: 200 OK
Expected Output: Response: 200 | Payload: {"status": "success"}
